1
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:04,060
But this is the goal of my journey.

2
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:09,130
To reunite with my friend
who departed ten years ago.

3
00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:19,020
Did you figure out where Gorilla went?

4
00:00:20,790 --> 00:00:22,130
Tür.

5
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:25,850
It's a trading city in the middle
of the northern lands.

6
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:28,140
That's a long ways east from here.

7
00:00:28,530 --> 00:00:31,400
It's in the opposite
direction from Äußerst.

8
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:33,470
Yeah.

9
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:47,710
Frieren, I came on this journey
to chase after Gorilla.

10
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:49,430
I know.

11
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:53,640
The sun's about to set.

12
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:56,180
Can't we wait until tomorrow
to make a decision?

13
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:01,250
I asked the village to lend us a cabin.

14
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:03,110
They said we can use it
however we want.

15
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:04,860
Thank you.

16
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:58,750
I got firewood.

17
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:02,210
I bought ingredients for dinner.

18
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:06,740
My hands are freezing.

19
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:09,450
It has gotten rather cold.

20
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:11,650
You're right.

21
00:03:11,650 --> 00:03:14,370
Wow, this might be a new record.

22
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:19,400
Let me see.

23
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:22,650
You're right. They're really cold.

24
00:03:22,650 --> 00:03:23,660
Right?

25
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:30,280
Don't!

26
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,410
Isn't this a new record?

27
00:03:32,410 --> 00:03:34,360
Yeah. They're freezing.

28
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:35,730
Ridiculous.

29
00:03:42,190 --> 00:03:43,790
It's snowing.

30
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:47,420
Will we need to wait
for winter to pass again?

31
00:03:47,890 --> 00:03:51,690
We won't be crossing any
steep mountains this time.

32
00:03:52,030 --> 00:03:55,300
Unless there's a serious blizzard,
we'll be fine.

33
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:02,420
It's blizzarding.

34
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:03,540
It sure is.

35
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:04,570
Yup.

36
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:08,610
In this region, cold waves
last an entire month.

37
00:04:08,610 --> 00:04:10,950
I wouldn't recommend venturing far.

38
00:04:11,450 --> 00:04:14,730
You can keep using the cabin for a while.

39
00:04:18,450 --> 00:04:21,150
What do you want to do, Sein?
Should we leave?

40
00:04:21,150 --> 00:04:23,590
Do you even need to ask?

41
00:04:23,590 --> 00:04:26,350
So we're stuck here until
the cold wave passes.

42
00:04:26,350 --> 00:04:27,720
That's what it sounds like.

43
00:04:28,470 --> 00:04:31,610
But there are bars and shops here, at least.

44
00:04:31,610 --> 00:04:33,530
This cabin's nice and large, too.

45
00:04:33,530 --> 00:04:36,690
It's a lot better than the mountain cabin
we stayed in before.

46
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:43,670
And most importantly, there's a magic shop
in this village run by a shady old man.

47
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:49,470
In my experience, shops like those
tend to have legendary-level spells.

48
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:53,590
Getting to take my time
exploring it is a big win.

49
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,550
Legendary-level spells?

50
00:04:56,550 --> 00:04:58,700
What kinds have you encountered so far?

51
00:05:00,210 --> 00:05:05,550
A spell to get rid of mold
and a spell to remove tough oil stains.

52
00:05:06,350 --> 00:05:07,700
Incredible.

53
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:12,860
Those spells are so convenient,
they changed my world.

54
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:15,310
They sound like a grandma's household wisdom.

55
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,580
In any case, the only thing
we can do now is wait.

56
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:22,660
We'll die if we underestimate
the winters of the northern lands.

57
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:28,560
Mr. Stark <i>did</i> nearly die
in the Schwer Mountains.

58
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:31,360
I'm from the northern lands.

59
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,960
I know that much.

60
00:05:35,390 --> 00:05:39,930
Anyway, sounds like we'll be staying
together for a while longer.

61
00:06:09,220 --> 00:06:11,770
The cold wave should be ending soon.

62
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:15,270
It won't be long before you adventurers
can finally continue on your journey.

63
00:06:15,270 --> 00:06:17,800
Yeah, you're right.

64
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:22,010
Wait. Didn't we spend most of our time apart?

65
00:06:23,510 --> 00:06:24,500
Sein.

66
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:27,140
Do you have a minute?

67
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:29,190
What is it, Frieren?

68
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:31,630
You don't often come to the tavern.

69
00:06:32,230 --> 00:06:36,080
Stark and Fern are acting strange.

70
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:39,440
I think they're fighting.
Could you mediate?

71
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:43,820
Sure, but why are you asking me?

72
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:46,700
Because mediating is a priest's job.

73
00:06:47,530 --> 00:06:48,660
Is it?

74
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:57,440
What a sorry state of affairs.

75
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,380
What happened here?

76
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:02,660
It's Mr. Stark's fault.

77
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:06,380
Yeah, it's all my fault.

78
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:09,100
We won't get anywhere like this.

79
00:07:11,910 --> 00:07:14,590
Join me in the other room, one at a time.

80
00:07:24,790 --> 00:07:27,690
So, what happened?

81
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:31,290
Remember how Fern touched my cheek

82
00:07:31,290 --> 00:07:34,540
with her cold hands when we
first arrived at the cabin?

83
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:36,720
Yeah, I remember that.

84
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:40,340
Today, when I paid her back in kind,

85
00:07:41,850 --> 00:07:43,680
she got upset.

86
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,080
What are you, a child?

87
00:07:47,530 --> 00:07:51,990
Of course girls don't like it when
you put your hands on their face.

88
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:55,460
Are you okay with leaving
things the way they are?

89
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:57,760
I'd like to make up with her.

90
00:07:58,220 --> 00:08:03,090
Stark. Unlike me, you're good at heart.

91
00:08:03,090 --> 00:08:05,260
Be honest, and tell her how you feel.

92
00:08:05,690 --> 00:08:09,860
If you want to make up,
then you have to tell her that.

93
00:08:10,170 --> 00:08:13,230
Frieren won't mediate for you.

94
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:19,070
I know. I'll apologize to Fern.

95
00:08:21,220 --> 00:08:23,460
Stark feels bad about what he did.

96
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:27,780
He's just a kid. He didn't mean any harm.

97
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:32,340
I know. I'm being stubborn.

98
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:33,780
I'd like to apologize to him.

99
00:08:34,670 --> 00:08:37,290
It was my fault to begin with.

100
00:08:37,730 --> 00:08:40,270
I don't mind that he touched me.

101
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:46,080
It's just... the arm he used to
restrain my shoulder was so strong.

102
00:08:48,170 --> 00:08:51,320
It scared me a little.

103
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:55,410
Do you not like Stark?

104
00:08:56,030 --> 00:08:58,480
Why would you ask that?

105
00:08:58,480 --> 00:08:59,940
Is that how it seems to you?

106
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:04,680
Then tell him you were scared and make up.

107
00:09:06,590 --> 00:09:08,430
Be gentler.

108
00:09:08,430 --> 00:09:09,880
I'm sorry.

109
00:09:14,570 --> 00:09:16,700
Just start dating already!

110
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:23,220
I'm not sure what happened,
but I think you're trying really hard, Sein.

111
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:26,610
Thanks for the help.

112
00:09:28,530 --> 00:09:33,630
Frieren, you're the only one
who praises me like I'm a kid.

113
00:09:33,630 --> 00:09:35,520
But you <i>are</i> a kid.

114
00:09:36,770 --> 00:09:39,270
I guess it's not so bad.

115
00:09:42,310 --> 00:09:45,530
You know, I've been wondering.

116
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:49,430
Why do you trouble yourself with me,

117
00:09:49,430 --> 00:09:52,580
like when you invited me to travel with you?

118
00:09:55,010 --> 00:09:57,530
Maybe it really is a dislike of my own kind.

119
00:09:58,090 --> 00:10:00,770
The way you refused to go on an adventure

120
00:10:00,770 --> 00:10:04,690
reminded me of myself before
I left to defeat the Demon King.

121
00:10:04,690 --> 00:10:06,000
It made me angry.

122
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:10,570
That doesn't explain why you
concern yourself with me.

123
00:10:10,570 --> 00:10:15,860
I think I wanted to give you a reason.

124
00:10:16,420 --> 00:10:17,840
What does that mean?

125
00:10:20,270 --> 00:10:23,570
It's what Himmel the Hero would've done.

126
00:10:26,070 --> 00:10:27,990
Take my hand, Frieren.

127
00:10:29,150 --> 00:10:32,080
I'll be your reason to go on a journey.

128
00:10:37,710 --> 00:10:41,070
They gave me the courage to travel

129
00:10:41,070 --> 00:10:44,190
and taught me the joy
of spending time with friends.

130
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:47,590
Well, Sein?

131
00:10:47,590 --> 00:10:49,220
Haven't you had fun?

132
00:10:52,010 --> 00:10:53,010
Yeah.

133
00:10:53,730 --> 00:10:55,660
This has been a lot of fun.

134
00:11:07,650 --> 00:11:11,610
I'm going to become
an unforgettable hero like Himmel.

135
00:11:12,010 --> 00:11:16,010
I'm talking about the present, Sein.

136
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:21,510
So I decided to trust her words.

137
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:26,360
Gorilla talked about you a lot.

138
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:31,840
He said the two of you would become heroes
whose names would be remembered forever.

139
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:58,950
I've decided to go after Gorilla.

140
00:11:59,490 --> 00:12:01,940
I won't live with regrets anymore.

141
00:12:02,670 --> 00:12:04,150
I know.

142
00:12:05,050 --> 00:12:06,540
Take care, then.

143
00:12:09,580 --> 00:12:10,470
See you later.

144
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:14,020
Later.

145
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:25,100
Well, that was a quick goodbye.

146
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:28,130
Unlike you two, Sein is an adult.

147
00:12:28,650 --> 00:12:30,360
I'm sure he'll be fine.

148
00:12:48,910 --> 00:12:51,890
It's so quiet traveling alone.

149
00:13:15,150 --> 00:13:16,030
Huh?

150
00:13:16,410 --> 00:13:19,530
That's unusual. They're still asleep.

151
00:13:20,180 --> 00:13:22,370
We've been walking a lot recently.

152
00:13:22,370 --> 00:13:23,920
Maybe they're tired.

153
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,860
Good enough.

154
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:46,780
Hey, breakfast is ready. Get up.

155
00:13:49,750 --> 00:13:50,760
Fern?

156
00:13:55,070 --> 00:13:57,360
Frieren, wake up.

157
00:13:58,470 --> 00:14:00,760
Just twelve more hours...

158
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:03,250
You can't sleep that long.

159
00:14:03,670 --> 00:14:06,010
More importantly, Fern doesn't look well.

160
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:11,680
Hey.

161
00:14:18,770 --> 00:14:20,440
Don't.

162
00:14:22,210 --> 00:14:24,630
You've got a fever.

163
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:27,360
You need to keep warm and rest.

164
00:14:29,690 --> 00:14:31,740
Let's see...

165
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:38,400
Huh? That's odd.

166
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:39,920
I brought water.

167
00:14:40,670 --> 00:14:41,750
Found it.

168
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:43,340
What is that?

169
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:47,730
Sein left us some notes on medicinal herbs.

170
00:14:47,730 --> 00:14:49,640
Sein did, huh?

171
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:54,220
I can use magic to identify her illness
and figure out which herbs to use.

172
00:14:54,640 --> 00:14:58,410
But I thought identifying illnesses
was magic of the Goddess.

173
00:14:58,410 --> 00:15:02,180
Didn't you say only the owner
of a holy scripture could cast it?

174
00:15:02,510 --> 00:15:05,270
I've got a holy scripture.

175
00:15:05,270 --> 00:15:05,900
What?

176
00:15:10,450 --> 00:15:12,480
You're using it as a pot stand!

177
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:20,140
I'm not cut out to be a priest,
but even I can identify simple illnesses.

178
00:15:20,630 --> 00:15:22,950
I can't identify complex ones, though.

179
00:15:22,950 --> 00:15:24,320
You sure you're okay?

180
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,720
Yeah. It's just a cold.

181
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:32,770
Which of the applicable herbs
are found in this region?

182
00:15:34,620 --> 00:15:35,960
Come to think of it,

183
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:40,010
there's a place nearby where I once
gathered herbs with Himmel and the others.

184
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:44,330
For now, let's head someplace
where we can get out of the cold.

185
00:15:44,910 --> 00:15:46,170
You're right.

186
00:15:57,750 --> 00:15:58,660
Oh?

187
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:08,660
You're a lifesaver.

188
00:16:08,910 --> 00:16:12,430
I didn't think anyone lived
this deep in the mountains.

189
00:16:12,430 --> 00:16:15,440
There was a whole village here
when I stopped by before.

190
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:18,130
That was decades ago.

191
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:23,350
It was a prestigious village
once visited by the hero.

192
00:16:23,830 --> 00:16:26,600
Anyway, make yourselves at home.

193
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:28,490
Thank you.

194
00:16:29,190 --> 00:16:33,030
By the way, isn't there an icicle
cherry blossom tree near here?

195
00:16:33,030 --> 00:16:35,610
Yes, north of here.

196
00:16:36,090 --> 00:16:38,920
It's a bit difficult to get there, though.

197
00:16:39,410 --> 00:16:40,650
It's all right.

198
00:16:41,070 --> 00:16:43,240
I've been here before.

199
00:16:45,110 --> 00:16:47,830
Well, I'll be working.

200
00:16:50,460 --> 00:16:51,950
Wait here, Fern.

201
00:16:52,430 --> 00:16:54,640
We'll gather the ingredients
we need for your medicine.

202
00:16:55,140 --> 00:16:57,950
You've been holding her hand
since we arrived.

203
00:16:58,480 --> 00:17:00,170
Because she seems to be in pain.

204
00:17:00,450 --> 00:17:05,240
When Fern has a cold,
holding her hand makes her feel better.

205
00:17:05,760 --> 00:17:07,900
She's been that way since she was a child.

206
00:17:11,620 --> 00:17:12,930
What's wrong?

207
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:17,690
Ms. Frieren, you're embarrassing me.

208
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,700
How?

209
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:24,000
Don't treat me like a child.

210
00:17:27,050 --> 00:17:29,700
I see. You're right.

211
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:36,710
In two years, she'll be a full-grown adult.

212
00:17:37,790 --> 00:17:41,290
It wasn't long ago that
she only came up to here.

213
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:44,910
I was way taller than her.

214
00:17:44,910 --> 00:17:46,650
But in the blink of an eye, she grew up.

215
00:17:47,270 --> 00:17:51,400
In my mind, Fern is still a child.

216
00:17:52,270 --> 00:17:55,500
I'll probably always think of her that way.

217
00:17:56,990 --> 00:17:58,480
Frieren...

218
00:17:59,180 --> 00:18:02,240
We'd better hurry and get those herbs.

219
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:07,420
Yeah.

220
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:34,930
We should be arriving at the
icicle cherry blossom tree soon.

221
00:18:34,930 --> 00:18:39,950
Is the icicle cherry blossom tree
the last ingredient we need for the medicine?

222
00:18:39,950 --> 00:18:43,820
We'll actually be using the mushrooms
that grow at the base of the tree.

223
00:18:57,470 --> 00:18:59,100
It's beautiful.

224
00:18:59,100 --> 00:19:01,270
I wish we could've showed Fern.

225
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:05,470
It might be my favorite flower
that blooms in winter.

226
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:09,480
Be careful. The flowers are poisonous.

227
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:14,740
Hey, why'd you hold Fern's hand?

228
00:19:15,310 --> 00:19:18,100
Normally you don't treat her
that much like a child.

229
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:21,470
I wasn't trying to treat her like a child.

230
00:19:22,230 --> 00:19:25,610
I simply held her hand because
it looked like she was in pain.

231
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:31,240
It's the only way I know to relieve her pain.

232
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:36,750
What should I have done?

233
00:19:39,110 --> 00:19:42,380
I guess you just have to do
what you want to do.

234
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:45,750
At least, that's what my master did.

235
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:50,790
People probably need emotional support.

236
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:55,350
Nobody dislikes receiving support.

237
00:20:01,810 --> 00:20:03,400
What do you think you're doing?

238
00:20:03,940 --> 00:20:05,680
You were moaning in your sleep.

239
00:20:06,270 --> 00:20:09,040
We feel helpless when we're sick.

240
00:20:09,610 --> 00:20:14,660
I lost my mother when I was young,
but she used to hold my hand like this.

241
00:20:15,330 --> 00:20:17,310
It's strangely calming.

242
00:20:17,310 --> 00:20:19,660
You mean when you were a child, right?

243
00:20:20,110 --> 00:20:24,150
It's not just children who
need emotional support.

244
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:28,130
It doesn't bother you, does it?

245
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:31,160
You're right.

246
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:34,200
I guess it's not so bad.

247
00:20:35,140 --> 00:20:38,380
I'm pretty handsome when
I'm being considerate, aren't I?

248
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:39,880
Please just be quiet.

249
00:20:42,010 --> 00:20:44,530
The medicine is ready.

250
00:20:47,710 --> 00:20:51,870
Fern was probably embarrassed
because I was there.

251
00:20:52,990 --> 00:20:57,100
Nobody likes to be seen acting
like a pampered child.

252
00:20:58,190 --> 00:21:00,170
Thank you, Stark.

253
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:03,690
I'll try doing what I want to do.

254
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:09,600
To thank you, I'll hold your hand
when you get sick.

255
00:21:10,010 --> 00:21:11,900
Don't. It's embarrassing.

256
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:16,900
Okay, let's gather some mushrooms.

257
00:21:17,590 --> 00:21:19,260
Hup.

258
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:22,280
They're bigger than I expected! Scary!

259
00:21:22,790 --> 00:21:25,770
Now we just add the other ingredients...

260
00:21:26,050 --> 00:21:29,040
And mix very, very well.

261
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:31,530
You're like a witch! Really scary!

262
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:36,050
Open your mouth, Fern.

263
00:21:45,290 --> 00:21:48,590
You're good at that. Thanks for the help.

264
00:21:49,040 --> 00:21:50,510
You think so?

265
00:21:52,010 --> 00:21:55,510
It's all right. You'll feel better soon.

266
00:21:56,060 --> 00:22:00,030
Ms. Frieren, I'm not a child anymore.

267
00:22:00,860 --> 00:22:01,900
I know.

268
00:22:02,730 --> 00:22:04,000
I know that.

269
00:22:14,110 --> 00:22:17,300
Take care of yourselves!

270
00:22:18,250 --> 00:22:21,310
Thank you so much!

271
00:22:21,830 --> 00:22:23,600
You're looking a lot better.

272
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:30,300
I have the two of you and
Mr. Sein's notes to thank for that.

273
00:22:30,300 --> 00:22:35,280
The owner of that home was very kind, too.

274
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:37,820
Okay.

275
00:22:38,720 --> 00:22:44,050
Our destination is Äußerst, the city of magic.

276
00:24:20,330 --> 00:24:22,830
Could I take a look at that?

277
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:21,810
Try it.

278
00:24:21,810 --> 00:24:24,620
Maybe I'll take a break.

279
00:24:22,100 --> 00:24:24,550
This year's test-takers
seem rather exceptional.

280
00:24:22,830 --> 00:24:24,330
You wanna fight, huh?

281
00:24:24,330 --> 00:24:26,460
I can't do this alone.

282
00:24:24,620 --> 00:24:27,250
You have the eyes of a killer.

283
00:24:25,130 --> 00:24:27,370
Don't call me an old mage.

284
00:24:26,460 --> 00:24:27,270
Dunno.

285
00:24:27,270 --> 00:24:30,600
The first-class mage exam will now begin.
